96404368c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-71268" :question/problem "Find a direction vector of the line that is given as the intersection of the planes $z=1$ and $x=y.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that: \n\n- For the plane $z=1$, a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨0,0,1⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $x=y$ (or $x-y=0$), a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨1,-1,0⟩.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & ={n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} \\\\  & =⟨0,0,1⟩\\times ⟨1,-1,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =i+j \\\\  & =⟨1,1,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-71268/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b5f51ee-5bde-5e39-8d2a-e5e482be4916"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-71268"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-71251/selection/e2847a0ad51c7771a4369851e9e16a5a3f66df58238aea0ccb766548161d9265" :answer/id #uuid "bf46c8a5-33f3-526a-9f51-cc90d167d3cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨2,-1,4⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71251/selection/b83b986eafeff0bd29fcb6bd60012048362301d0d834c9d73cdb597237dc9b2b" :answer/id #uuid "bdbb16e7-a03e-5861-ac67-26d1fa111640" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-3,-2,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71251/selection/045c9df6f37523e76ad186d71395ffab66c5af2ca19cb944d1d427bdd1c29ce3" :answer/id #uuid "79364c79-ba80-5f61-a84c-9ccc26656702" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-1,-2,-2⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71251/selection/aa3ff83b8a1f1cf3a730026b6043228db7130af4209594135971571193be91de" :answer/id #uuid "3a2f075d-7b05-5e6a-985a-6ddffd332a62" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨2,-1,0⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71251/selection/b7190f6325ba0997800e902c4bc0e2fcd