{:db/id "q-129170" :question/id #uuid "2f626f64-b605-58e9-8e55-f56146c3feb3" :question/math-academy-id "q-129170" :question/problem "Find a direction vector of the line that is given as the intersection of the following two planes:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-3x+4z-11=0 \\\\ x-2y+31=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we notice:\n\n- For the plane $-3x+4z-11=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨-3,0,4⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $x-2y+31=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨1,-2,0⟩.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & ={n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} \\\\  & =⟨-3,0,4⟩\\times ⟨1,-2,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -3 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =8i+4j+6k \\\\  & =⟨8,4,6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-129170/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b5f51ee-5bde-5e39-8d2a-e5e482be4916"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-129170"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-71260/selection/826a420d56563e9552cac2d5d072ccd8cfe0d364279143aacd60dcd14d24a0a8" :answer/id #uuid "b0bba63b-484c-5630-8ed5-53736d94d609" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-12,4,-8⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71260/selection/4156d65a09e772b876803ea73dac4866999832d73be044342dc25c05d51ee975" :answer/id #uuid "0d83a033-b0bb-5438-9f8c-28682bfe8259" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,4,2⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71260/selection/c4857571cea42be8fe5f356d51d8847a9090fe6753e2e6551957c1d0732ae7c8" :answer/id #uuid "5cda850d-37a2-5cea-8236-54a98a8db142" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨4,2,-1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71260/selection/74202d719215e2101888228a911805a672de2c431d046b38837a6e8e7905c4a5" :answer/id #uuid "dc3b5358-8006-5f3d-bd4c-0610a60bd282" :answer/